# Continuum production build-time env.
#
# Copy to .env.production and edit before `npm run build` when installing on
# a VPS. For an agent-less static demo, OMIT VITE_AGENT_URL entirely (or build
# with no .env.production) — agent.js short-circuits every /api call into
# offline mode when the variable is ABSENT.
#
# Three configured values (FE-06 fixes the old "empty == offline" conflation):
#
#   VITE_AGENT_URL=/continuum   → VPS at https://example.com/continuum
#   VITE_AGENT_URL=             → VPS at https://example.com (root_app, no subpath)
#   VITE_AGENT_URL=https://api.example.com → cross-origin API (rare)
#
# An explicit EMPTY value (VITE_AGENT_URL=) is a valid root mount, NOT offline.
# An ABSENT value is the offline demo. The Ansible installer sets this
# automatically based on inventory vars.

VITE_AGENT_URL=/continuum